---
import ToolPage from '../../../layouts/ToolPage.astro';

const steps = [
  'Paste your CSS on the left: whole rules like <code>.card { … }</code>, or just an element’s inline style like <code>padding: 16px; color: #333</code>. Or start with the example.',
  'The preview at the top draws the same element twice, once with your CSS and once with the Tailwind classes, so you can see they match. Hover it to check hover styles too.',
  'Copy the classes for each element and paste them into <code>class</code> (or <code>className</code>). Amber classes are exact values in square brackets: they work, but they aren’t part of Tailwind’s scale.',
];

const faq = [
  { q: 'Does it handle every CSS property?', a: 'No, and we’d rather be honest about it. It handles the common things: spacing, sizes, colors, text, flex and grid, borders, rounded corners, shadows, hover and focus states, and <code>@media</code> breakpoints. Anything else is kept exactly as written in square brackets, like <code>[mask-type:luminance]</code>, which Tailwind also accepts.' },
  { q: 'What do the amber classes mean?', a: 'They’re exact values in square brackets, like <code>p-[18px]</code> or <code>bg-[#2563eb]</code>, used because nothing on Tailwind’s scale matched. They work fine. If you see a lot of them, your design may use its own spacing or colors, and adding them to your Tailwind theme keeps things tidy.' },
  { q: 'Why did my color become a Tailwind color like blue-600?', a: 'When your color is so close to a Tailwind color that people can’t tell them apart (difference under 2.5), we use the Tailwind name. Those classes have a dotted underline. Tick <strong>Snap colors to Tailwind</strong> to always use the nearest Tailwind color, even when it’s further away.' },
  { q: 'v4 or v3?', a: 'If your CSS file starts with <code>@import "tailwindcss";</code> and there’s no <code>tailwind.config.js</code>, you’re on v4. If you have a <code>tailwind.config.js</code>, you’re on v3. Some names changed between them (v3’s <code>shadow</code> is v4’s <code>shadow-sm</code>, for example), and v4 changed the exact color shades.' },
  { q: 'How are @media queries turned into prefixes?', a: '<code>min-width: 640px</code>, <code>768px</code>, <code>1024px</code>, <code>1280px</code> and <code>1536px</code> become <code>sm:</code>, <code>md:</code>, <code>lg:</code>, <code>xl:</code> and <code>2xl:</code>. Other widths become <code>min-[900px]:</code>. <code>max-width</code> becomes <code>max-sm:</code> and friends, dark mode becomes <code>dark:</code>.' },
  { q: 'What about selectors like .card:hover .title?', a: 'That becomes <code>group-hover:</code> on <code>.title</code>, and the tool tells you to add the class <code>group</code> to <code>.card</code>. Other complex selectors are listed under the element they style.' },
  { q: 'Is my CSS uploaded?', a: 'No. Everything runs in your browser.' },
];
---
<ToolPage
  slug="css-to-tailwind"
  title="CSS to Tailwind converter, with a live preview · Darnly"
  description="Paste CSS and get Tailwind classes for each selector, with hover, focus and @media breakpoints. A live side-by-side preview shows they match. v4 and v3. Free."
  h1="CSS to Tailwind converter"
  lede="Paste CSS and get the Tailwind classes for each element. The preview draws your CSS and the Tailwind version side by side, so you can see they look the same before you copy."
  steps={steps}
  faq={faq}
>
  <div class="ct">
    <div class="pick" id="ct-pick" role="tablist" aria-label="Element to preview"></div>
    <div class="stage" aria-label="Your CSS and the Tailwind version, drawn side by side">
      <figure class="pane">
        <figcaption>Your CSS</figcaption>
        <div class="canvas" id="ct-a"></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="pane">
        <figcaption>Tailwind classes</figcaption>
        <div class="canvas" id="ct-b"></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="verdict" id="ct-verdict" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <ul class="diffs" id="ct-diffs" hidden></ul>

    <div class="grid">
      <div class="side">
        <div class="head">
          <label for="ct-input" class="lab">Your CSS</label>
          <div class="head-btns">
            <button id="ct-example" type="button" class="ghost">Example</button>
            <button id="ct-clear" type="button" class="ghost">Clear</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <textarea id="ct-input" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off" placeholder=".card { padding: 24px; border-radius: 12px; }"></textarea>
        <p class="bad" id="ct-error" role="alert" hidden></p>
      </div>

      <div class="side">
        <div class="head">
          <span class="lab">Tailwind classes</span>
          <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Tailwind version">
            <button type="button" data-version="v4" aria-pressed="true">v4</button>
            <button type="button" data-version="v3" aria-pressed="false">v3</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="ct-snap" /> Snap colors to Tailwind (use the nearest Tailwind color, even if it’s not close)</label>
        <ol class="out" id="ct-out"></ol>
        <p class="empty" id="ct-empty">Paste some CSS and the classes appear here.</p>
        <p class="legend">
          <span class="k exact">clean</span> on Tailwind’s scale
          <span class="k near">close</span> nearest Tailwind value
          <span class="k arbitrary">exact value</span> in square brackets
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="actions">
      <button id="ct-all" type="button" class="ghost">Copy all</button>
      <button id="ct-prompt" type="button" class="primary">Copy prompt for your AI agent</button>
      <p class="status" id="ct-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </div>

    <details class="more">
      <summary>See each line</summary>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Your CSS</th><th>Tailwind</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody id="ct-table"></tbody>
      </table>
    </details>
  </div>
</ToolPage>

<script>
  import '../../../scripts/css-to-tailwind';
</script>

<style>
  [hidden] { display: none !important; }
  .ct { display: grid; gap: 20px; min-width: 0; }
  .ct [hidden] { display: none !important; }
  .pick { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; }
  .pick:empty { display: none; }
  .pick :global(button) { font: 500 14px/1 var(--mono); padding: 9px 12px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--white); color: var(--ink); cursor: pointer; max-width: 100%; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pick :global(button[aria-selected='true']) { background: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--white); }
  .stage { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 12px; padding: 12px; border-radius: 24px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--wash); }
  .pane { margin: 0; display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; gap: 8px; min-width: 0; }
  .pane figcaption { font: 700 12px/1 var(--mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--ink-soft); padding: 4px 6px 0; }
  /* Each canvas is its own little page: position:fixed stays inside it, nothing spills out. */
  .canvas { position: relative; transform: translateZ(0); overflow: auto; contain: paint; min-height: 260px; display: grid; place-items: center; padding: 28px 20px; border-radius: 16px; background-color: #fff; background-image: radial-gradient(rgba(11, 34, 48, 0.08) 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 16px 16px; color: #111; font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; }
  .canvas :global(.ct-sample) { box-sizing: border-box; min-width: 0; max-width: 100%; border: 0 solid currentColor; }
  .canvas :global(.ct-item) { box-sizing: border-box; padding: 6px 10px; border: 1.5px dashed rgba(11, 34, 48, 0.3); border-radius: 6px; font-size: 14px; }
  .verdict { margin: -6px 0 0; font: 600 18px/1.4 var(--body); }
  .verdict:global(.ok) { color: #0B6B3A; }
  .verdict:global(.warn) { color: #8A5A00; }
  .diffs { margin: -10px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .diffs :global(code) { font: 13px var(--mono); }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 28px; align-items: start; }
  .side { display: grid; gap: 12px; min-width: 0; }
  .head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
  .lab { font-weight: 600; }
  .head-btns { display: flex; gap: 8px; }
  .ghost { font: 600 14px/1 var(--body); padding: 10px 16px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--white); color: var(--ink); cursor: pointer; }
  .ghost:hover { border-color: var(--sky); }
  .primary { font: 600 15px/1 var(--body); padding: 12px 20px; border-radius: 999px; border: 0; background: var(--pink); color: var(--white); cursor: pointer; }
  textarea { width: 100%; min-height: 380px; font: 400 13px/1.6 var(--mono); font-variant-ligatures: none; padding: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--white); color: var(--ink); resize: vertical; tab-size: 2; }
  textarea:focus { outline: 3px solid var(--pink); outline-offset: 1px; }
  .bad { margin: 0; padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 12px; background: #FDF3E1; color: #6B4600; font-size: 14px; }
  .seg { display: inline-flex; gap: 2px; padding: 3px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--wash); }
  .seg button { font: 600 14px/1 var(--mono); padding: 8px 14px; border: 0; border-radius: 999px; background: none; color: var(--ink); cursor: pointer; }
  .seg button[aria-pressed='true'] { background: var(--ink); color: var(--white); }
  .check { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .check input { margin-top: 3px; }
  .out { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  .out :global(li) { display: grid; gap: 8px; padding: 12px 14px; border-radius: 14px; background: var(--ink); color: #D9EEF6; min-width: 0; }
  .out :global(.row) { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
  .out :global(.sel) { font: 600 13px/1.3 var(--mono); color: #8FB4C4; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .out :global(.copy) { flex: none; font: 600 13px/1 var(--body); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 8px; border: 0; background: var(--sky); color: var(--white); cursor: pointer; }
  .out :global(.cls) { margin: 0; font: 400 14px/1.8 var(--mono); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .out :global(.note) { margin: 0; font-size: 13px; color: #F5D38A; }
  .out :global(.t) { white-space: nowrap; }
  .out :global(.t.near) { text-decoration: underline dotted rgba(217, 238, 246, 0.6); text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .out :global(.t.arbitrary) { color: #FFC24B; }
  .empty { margin: 0; padding: 40px 20px; border: 2px dashed var(--line); border-radius: 16px; color: var(--ink-soft); text-align: center; }
  .legend { margin: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 6px 10px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .k { font: 600 12px/1 var(--mono); padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--ink); color: #D9EEF6; }
  .k.near { text-decoration: underline dotted; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .k.arbitrary { color: #FFC24B; }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 12px; }
  .status { margin: 0; min-height: 1.6em; font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .more { padding: 4px 20px; border-radius: 16px; background: var(--wash); min-width: 0; }
  .more summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; padding: 12px 0; }
  .more table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font: 13px/1.4 var(--mono); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .more th, .more :global(td) { text-align: left; vertical-align: top; padding: 6px 8px 6px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .more th { font: 600 13px/1.3 var(--body); color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .more :global(td.arbitrary) { color: #8A5A00; }
  .more :global(td.n) { font-family: var(--body); color: var(--ink-soft); }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .stage { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .canvas { min-height: 200px; }
    .more { overflow-x: auto; }
  }
</style>
